From: Altium-on-Wine kit
Subject: winemac: don't attach owned windows to a zero-size owner

Modules: dlls/winemac.drv
Base: wine-11.16 (applies to stock source and to the kit's patched tree)

Wine makes an owned window a Cocoa child of its owner's window. macOS keeps a child
window on its parent's display, and with "Displays have separate Spaces" (the default)
it isn't drawn on any other display. Delphi programs such as Altium own every dialog,
panel and dropdown by a hidden 0x0 application window, which Wine shows as a 1x1
window in the middle of the main display. So with Altium on another monitor, its
workspace dropdown ("Not Connected") and other popups were ordered in and focused but
never drawn: they only flashed. A zero-size owner has nothing on screen to keep its
owned windows above, so its owned windows get no Cocoa parent.

--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/window.c
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/window.c
@@ -270,6 +270,18 @@
     owner = NtUserGetWindowRelative(data->hwnd, GW_OWNER);
     if (owner)
         owner = NtUserGetAncestor(owner, GA_ROOT);
+    if (owner)
+    {
+        /* A Cocoa child window stays on its parent's display (with "Displays have
+           separate Spaces", it isn't drawn anywhere else). A zero-size owner, such
+           as the hidden application window of Delphi programs (Altium), has
+           nothing on screen to keep its owned windows above, so don't attach them
+           to it: they would only show on the display that holds its 1x1 window. */
+        RECT rect;
+        if (NtUserGetWindowRect(owner, &rect, NtUserGetDpiForWindow(owner)) &&
+            (rect.right <= rect.left || rect.bottom <= rect.top))
+            owner = 0;
+    }
     owner_win = macdrv_get_cocoa_window(owner, TRUE);
     macdrv_set_cocoa_parent_window(data->cocoa_window, owner_win);
 
